1
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,840
China makes too many cars and the world is increasingly okay with it.
中国生产的汽车太多了，而世界对此越来越接受。

2
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:44,200
That's how Bloomberg frames China's car exports.
这是彭博社对中国汽车出口的描述。

3
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:50,200
According to the latest data from the China Association of Automobile Manufacturers, total
根据中国汽车工业协会的最新数据，

4
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:57,079
vehicle exports in the first two months of this year reached over 1.35 million units,
今年前两个月整车出口达到135万辆以上，同比增长近50%。

5
00:00:57,079 --> 00:01:00,719
marking a year-on-year increase of nearly 50%.
这意味着中国每小时出口近1000辆汽车。

6
00:01:00,719 --> 00:01:06,879
That's almost 1,000 new cars exported from China every hour.
新能源汽车引领了增长，出口量占总量的40%以上。

7
00:01:06,879 --> 00:01:14,759
New energy vehicles, or N.E.V.s, led the surge, with exports accounting for more than 40% of the total.
每小时有近400辆新能源汽车驶离中国。如何理解这些数字？

8
00:01:14,759 --> 00:01:19,039
Every hour, almost 400 N.E.V.s depart China.
是什么推动了这种超高速增长？为什么中国汽车越来越受欢迎？

9
00:01:19,039 --> 00:01:21,120
How to make sense of these numbers?
欢迎收看本期《对话》，我是刘欣，一档来自北京的评论节目。

10
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:24,039
What's fueling this hyper-accelerated growth?
很高兴请到中国深圳的卡尔·费，奥斯陆挪威商学院战略学教授。

11
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:28,920
Why are Chinese vehicles increasingly embraced around the world?
美国明尼阿波利斯的邢磊，播客《中国电动车与更多》的联合主持人。

12
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:34,280
Welcome to this edition of The Point with me, Liu Xin, an opinion show coming to you live from Beijing.
以及演播室的李伦，北京大学经济学助理教授。热烈欢迎各位。

13
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:39,760
I'm pleased to be joined from Shenzhen, Southern China, by Carl Fei, Professor of Strategy
首先，让我们仔细看看这些数字。

14
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:43,400
at BI Norwegian Business School in Oslo.
2026年前两个月，中国出口了135万辆汽车，同比增长近50%。

15
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:50,320
From Minneapolis, the U.S., by Xing Lei, co-host of the podcast China E.V.s and More.
新能源汽车占总量的40%以上，约60万辆，同比增长110%。

16
00:01:50,319 --> 00:01:55,799
And here in the studio by Li Luan, Assistant Professor of Economics at Peking University.
传统燃油汽车出口增长了22%。我先请卡尔教授来谈谈。

17
00:01:55,799 --> 00:01:58,359
The warmest welcome to all of you gentlemen.
我们看到了什么？我认为我们看到世界各地的电动车越来越受欢迎。

18
00:01:58,359 --> 00:02:02,119
First of all, let's take a closer look at the numbers.
最初人们对购买昂贵的中国产品持怀疑态度，担心质量。

19
00:02:02,119 --> 00:02:09,400
Now in the first two months of 2026, China exported 1.3 million, 1.35 million vehicles,
但他们发现中国的电动车实际上质量非常好。

20
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:12,639
an increase of almost 50% year-on-year, as I said.
这现在给了人们信心。

21
00:02:12,639 --> 00:02:19,400
And N.E.V. cars account for over 40% of that, some 600,000 units.
中国汽车出口持续增长，

22
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:24,400
That's an increase of 110% year-on-year.
反映了全球市场对中国制造的认可。

23
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:32,120
Meanwhile, traditional combustion engine vehicle exports grew by 22%.
新能源汽车是这一增长的主要驱动力。

24
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:35,680
So let me go to Professor Carl Fei there.
中国在电动车领域的技术优势正在转化为市场优势。

25
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:37,319
What are we seeing?
未来几年这一趋势将继续保持。

26
00:02:37,319 --> 00:02:44,099
Well, I think we're seeing, you know, EVs around the world becoming more popular.
中国汽车品牌的国际影响力不断提升。

27
00:02:44,099 --> 00:02:52,180
I think initially people were somewhat skeptical to buy a Chinese product that was so expensive,
这对全球汽车产业格局产生了深远影响。

28
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:54,479
wondering if the quality would be there.
中国制造的品质已经得到广泛认可。

29
00:02:54,479 --> 00:02:59,099
But they're seeing that Chinese EVs actually are really quite good.
我们期待更多创新成果。

30
00:02:59,099 --> 00:03:00,599
And this is...
中国汽车业正在引领全球绿色转型。

